const e={readingNotes:[{title:{zh:"研究问题",en:"Research question"},body:{zh:"论文围绕股票拆分信息研究价格如何在事件时间内调整，展示早期事件研究的组织方式。 阅读时先把它理解为一个被界定的问题，而不是可以脱离样本、时间和制度环境的结论。",en:"“The Adjustment of Stock Prices to New Information” frames a bounded research question. Read the stated question together with the named sample, dates, and institutional setting rather than treating it as a conclusion that automatically travels to another market or period."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.2307/2525569",label:{zh:"International Economic Review (1969) · 来源说明",en:"International Economic Review (1969) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"研究设计",en:"Research design"},body:{zh:"来源把事件、收益和市场比较放入事件窗口，重点是信息时点与正常回报基准的定义。 这说明比较对象、观察窗口和对照关系是研究合同的一部分；改变其中任何一项，都可能改变所检验的命题。",en:"For “The Adjustment of Stock Prices to New Information”, the source describes a deliberate comparison, observation window, and control relation. Those choices are part of its research contract: changing one can change the proposition being tested, even when the method label remains the same."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.2307/2525569",label:{zh:"International Economic Review (1969) · 来源说明",en:"International Economic Review (1969) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"数据与时点",en:"Data and timing"},body:{zh:"需要原始公告时间、拆分与股息资料、复权价格、市场指数、交易日历和事件样本筛选规则。 数据字段、可得时点和样本筛选需要与原始研究分开记录，不能仅凭同名变量或最终修订数据就视为可比。",en:"For “The Adjustment of Stock Prices to New Information”, keep the fields, their availability timing, and the sample filters separate from the original study. A same-named variable, later-revised database, or matching end-of-period date is not automatically a comparable input."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.2307/2525569",label:{zh:"International Economic Review (1969) · 来源说明",en:"International Economic Review (1969) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"如何理解结果",en:"How to read the result"},body:{zh:"该研究说明事件时间分析依赖准确的事件和基准构造，而不是说明每一条新闻都会产生同一种价格反应。 它支持的是该来源所描述的经验或理论关系；它本身不把相关性、模型拟合或历史表现升级为因果、可执行性或未来保证。",en:"For “The Adjustment of Stock Prices to New Information”, the source supports only the empirical or theoretical relation it describes. It does not turn association, model fit, or historical performance into causality, a directly executable procedure, or a guarantee about subsequent outcomes."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.2307/2525569",label:{zh:"International Economic Review (1969) · 来源说明",en:"International Economic Review (1969) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"复核清单",en:"Replication checks"},body:{zh:"区分公告、传闻、实施和交易所生效日期，处理事件重叠和停牌，并保存使用的复权及基准版本。 在做后续分析前，应把这些选择写入版本化的研究记录，并保留原始来源链接与访问日期。",en:"Before extending “The Adjustment of Stock Prices to New Information”, record its sample, timing, construction choices, and source edition in a versioned note. Keep the primary-source link and access date so a later reader can distinguish a changed definition from a changed result."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.2307/2525569",label:{zh:"International Economic Review (1969) · 来源说明",en:"International Economic Review (1969) · source description"}}},{title:{zh:"适用边界",en:"Scope boundary"},body:{zh:"该条导读引用 International Economic Review (1969)。历史股票拆分样本和市场制度不等于当前事件的因果模板；该导读不输出异常收益或交易信号。 若需要量化结论、参数、表格或稳健性检验，请回到原文并单独核对版本、附录与样本定义。",en:"This guide cites International Economic Review (1969) for “The Adjustment of Stock Prices to New Information”. Its public description defines the boundary. For numerical conclusions, parameters, tables, or robustness tests, return to the original and separately verify the edition, appendices, and sample definitions."},reference:{url:"https://doi.org/10.2307/2525569",label:{zh:"International Economic Review (1969) · 来源说明",en:"International Economic Review (1969) · source description"}}}],readerLimits:{zh:"本文只整理“The Adjustment of Stock Prices to New Information”所公开说明的研究问题与设计边界，不构成收益预测、交易规则或全文复现。历史股票拆分样本和市场制度不等于当前事件的因果模板；该导读不输出异常收益或交易信号。",en:"This guide only organizes the publicly described question and design of “The Adjustment of Stock Prices to New Information”. It is not a return forecast, trading rule, or full-text replication. The source's stated scope remains controlling."}};export{e as default};
